From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomasz Pakuła <tomasz.pakula.oficjalny@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Jan 2026 21:31:41 +0000
Subject: Input: Add EVIOCGBTNCNT

Allow userspace to get the button count of input
devices. currently only used for Joysticks which
includes Simracing and Simflight hardware. Such
devices are always defined as generic joysticks.

Signed-off-by: Tomasz Pakuła <tomasz.pakula.oficjalny@gmail.com>

[ORDER 15: carried unchanged from Tomasz Pakuła's "[RFC PATCH n/6] Input: New EV_BTN event for generic buttons", linux-input and LKML, 2026-01-04 (the newest posted version; no v2 by 2026-11-06, not in torvalds/linux master of 2026-11-06).
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260104213132.163904-1-tomasz.pakula.oficjalny@gmail.com/
Archive copy of this patch: https://lkml.iu.edu/2601.0/01924.html
Review so far: Benjamin Tissoires 2026-01-08 asks for a different shape of patches 3 and 4 (map the HID Button usage page to EV_BTN directly, EV_BTN only for that page, keep the existing EV_KEY mapping without the upper bound); Peter Hutterer 2026-01-08 and Randy Dunlap 2026-01-04 (documentation wording of patch 1); Ivan Gorinov 2026-01-07 (EVIOCGKEY-like read of the initial state). The author has not posted a revision; this group is the text as posted and is replaced by the author's next version when it is posted.
Applies to v7.3.1 without change of any hunk.
Drop this group when the series, in the author's or the maintainers' final form, is in the release this kernel moves to.]
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
 drivers/input/evdev.c      | 5 +++++
 include/uapi/linux/input.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/evdev.c b/drivers/input/evdev.c
index 90ff6be85cf4..b90dc035c0b3 100644
--- a/drivers/input/evdev.c
+++ b/drivers/input/evdev.c
@@ -1134,6 +1134,11 @@ static long evdev_do_ioctl(struct file *file, unsigned int cmd,
 
 	case EVIOCSKEYCODE_V2:
 		return evdev_handle_set_keycode_v2(dev, p);
+
+	case EVIOCGBTNCNT:
+		if (copy_to_user(p, &dev->button_count, sizeof(unsigned int)))
+			return -EFAULT;
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	size = _IOC_SIZE(cmd);
diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/input.h b/include/uapi/linux/input.h
index 6aa703fcfcfb..3d1b17ebcdfc 100644
--- a/include/uapi/linux/input.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/input.h
@@ -174,6 +174,7 @@ struct input_mask {
 #define EVIOCGLED(len)		_IOC(_IOC_READ, 'E', 0x19, len)		/* get all LEDs */
 #define EVIOCGSND(len)		_IOC(_IOC_READ, 'E', 0x1a, len)		/* get all sounds status */
 #define EVIOCGSW(len)		_IOC(_IOC_READ, 'E', 0x1b, len)		/* get all switch states */
+#define EVIOCGBTNCNT		_IOR('E', 0x1c, unsigned int)		/* get button count */
 
 #define EVIOCGBIT(ev,len)	_IOC(_IOC_READ, 'E', 0x20 + (ev), len)	/* get event bits */
 #define EVIOCGABS(abs)		_IOR('E', 0x40 + (abs), struct input_absinfo)	/* get abs value/limits */
-- 
